    "content": "Delete some active workloads or streams to free up memory. Use the \"statistics show -object workload -counter ops\" command to determine which workloads are active. Active workloads show non-zero ops. Then use the \"workload delete <workload_name>\" command multiple times to remove specific workloads. Alternatively, use the \"stream delete -workload <workload name> *\" command to delete the associated streams from the active workload.\n\n${metric_or_resource.labels}",
